  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1229 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nThe cold front mentioned above arrives Tuesday morning and should \nexit the region by early Tuesday afternoon. Since this front will \narrive before peak heating, instability will be lacking, however, \nthere is enough deep layer shear to warrant a Marginal Risk (Level 1 \nof 5) along and west of the I-35 Corridor Monday night into Tuesday \nmorning. The primary hazards would be large hail and damaging wind. \nStorms should move through quick enough to limit any sort of \nflooding risk. Winds will ramp up a bit behind the front, but won't \nbe nearly as strong as our front a couple weeks ago. Drier air will \nmove in behind this front, setting the stage for a beautiful second \nhalf of the week with cool, crisp mornings in the 40s and 50s and \nafternoons in the 70s. Another front may approach by the end of the \nweek, but for now, this front looks dry.",
